{
  "//": [
    "Tool-call hooks. Copy this file to hooks.json (same directory) and edit.",
    "",
    "A hook is a shell command run around a tool call. The call's JSON is written",
    "to the hook's stdin: {session_id, cwd, hook_event_name, tool_name, tool_input,",
    "tool_response}. MNEMOAI_HOOK_EVENT and MNEMOAI_TOOL_NAME are also exported, so",
    "a one-liner needn't parse JSON at all.",
    "",
    "Events (this release): PreToolUse (before the call), PostToolUse (after a",
    "successful one), PostToolUseFailure (after one that raised).",
    "",
    "'matcher' is a glob over the tool name ('*' matches every tool). Every hook",
    "whose matcher matches runs, in the order written.",
    "",
    "What a hook's exit code and stdout mean:",
    "  exit 0            -> the call proceeds. Plain stdout is shown to you and",
    "                       logged, NOT sent to the model.",
    "  exit 2            -> DENY: the call is blocked and stderr is handed to the",
    "                       model as the reason.",
    "  any other code    -> non-blocking error: logged, the call proceeds.",
    "  timeout           -> non-blocking: logged, the call proceeds (a slow hook",
    "                       must not be able to wedge your edits).",
    "  JSON on stdout    -> honored: {\"decision\": \"deny\"|\"allow\", \"reason\": ...,",
    "                       \"additionalContext\": ...}. additionalContext IS sent to",
    "                       the model, appended to the tool result.",
    "",
    "'decision': 'allow' satisfies the confirmation prompt for that one call — it",
    "cannot reach past plan mode or the server-side safety floors, which block",
    "catastrophic commands and system-path writes no matter what a hook says.",
    "'deny' is honored everywhere.",
    "",
    "This file is read ONLY from the app home and is snapshotted at startup: hooks",
    "are arbitrary code, so a hooks.json arriving with a git clone must never fire,",
    "and an edit mid-session must never change what is running. Restart to apply.",
    "",
    "Hooks run on tool-calling threads (parallel sub-agents included), so they must",
    "be thread-safe and must never wait for input — a hook that prompts hangs on a",
    "terminal it doesn't have.",
    "",
    "Delete the '//' keys below (they are ignored, but they are noise in a live file)."
  ],

  "hooks": {
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "fs_write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python -c \"import json,sys,subprocess; p=json.load(sys.stdin).get('tool_input',{}).get('path',''); p.endswith('.py') and subprocess.run(['ruff','format',p])\"",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "file_edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python -c \"import json,sys,subprocess; p=json.load(sys.stdin).get('tool_input',{}).get('file_path',''); p.endswith('.py') and subprocess.run(['ruff','format',p])\"",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "//": "Deny any write under a directory you never want touched.",
        "matcher": "fs_write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python -c \"import json,sys; p=json.load(sys.stdin).get('tool_input',{}).get('path',''); sys.exit(0) if '/secrets/' not in p else (sys.stderr.write('Writes under /secrets/ are blocked by a local hook.'), sys.exit(2))\"",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "//": "Auto-approve read-only git commands so they stop prompting.",
        "matcher": "execute_bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python -c \"import json,sys; c=json.load(sys.stdin).get('tool_input',{}).get('command','').strip(); print(json.dumps({'decision':'allow'}) if c.startswith(('git status','git log','git diff')) else '')\"",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "PostToolUseFailure": [
      {
        "//": "Tell the model something it can act on when a tool raised.",
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "echo '{\"additionalContext\": \"A tool just failed. Re-read the file before retrying — it may have changed on disk.\"}'",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
